.TH START-LIBRESPOT 1 "2026-09-28" "HiFiBerry" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
start-librespot \- Librespot startup script for HiFiBerry devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start-librespot
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B start-librespot
is a startup script that handles the initialization of librespot with system-specific
configuration for HiFiBerry devices. It automatically configures audio parameters
based on the detected sound card and uses the system's pretty hostname.
.PP
The script sets up librespot with a default bitrate of 320 kbps and uses the ALSA
audio backend. It attempts to get the system's pretty hostname, falling back to
the regular hostname, and finally to "HiFiBerry" if neither is available.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VOLUME_CTRL
Selects librespot's volume control curve: one of
.IR linear ", " log ", " cubic " or " fixed .
Defaults to
.I linear
(unchanged behaviour). Set it via a systemd drop-in, e.g.
.I Environment=VOLUME_CTRL=cubic ,
for a more naturally curved Spotify Connect volume slider.
.TP
.B SYSTEM_CACHE
Directory where librespot persists its Spotify credentials and volume, so the
player can re-authenticate after a restart instead of waiting for a client to
push credentials over zeroconf again. Defaults to
.I ~/.librespot
when running as a user service, and to
.I /var/lib/librespot
otherwise. Set it via a systemd drop-in, e.g.
.I Environment=SYSTEM_CACHE=/var/lib/hifiberry/librespot ,
or to an empty value to disable persistence. This is not the audio cache,
which stays disabled.
.IP
The directory holds Spotify credentials, so its mode is set to 0700 on every
start. If it cannot be created, or its mode cannot be set \(em on a device
upgraded from 0.7.1.1 or earlier
.I /var/lib/librespot
still belongs to the retired
.B librespot
system user \(em a warning is logged and the player starts without
persistence.
.IP
When Spotify explicitly rejects the cached credentials (bad credentials,
credentials that cannot be validated, or an account without Premium),
librespot exits without touching them, and every restart would fail the same
way. The script therefore renames
.I credentials.json
to
.I credentials.json.rejected
when librespot reports such a rejection, so the next start falls back to
zeroconf discovery and a Spotify client can select the player again. Network
and audio failures, or any other exit, leave the credentials in place. This
only applies when the player logs in from the cache, not with a token from
audiocontrol.
.IP
To forget the cached credentials by hand, stop the service and remove
.I credentials.json
from the directory.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/hostname
.RS
System hostname configuration
.RE
.PP
.I ~/.librespot
.RS
Credentials and volume persisted by librespot, when running as a user service
.RE
.PP
.I /var/lib/librespot
.RS
Same, when not running as a user service
.RE
.PP
.I credentials.json.rejected
.RS
Cached credentials last rejected by Spotify, kept in the same directory for
inspection. Safe to remove.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR librespot (1),
.BR hostnamectl (1),
.BR spotify-event (1)
